(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test02_2A"] = [{"id":"9e501aaf","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Research conducted by planetary scientist Katarina Miljkovic suggests that the Moon’s surface may not accurately ______ early impact events. When the Moon was still forming, its surface was softer, and asteroid or meteoroid impacts would have left less of an impression; thus, evidence of early impacts may no longer be present.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Research conducted by planetary scientist Katarina Miljkovic suggests that the Moon’s surface may not accurately ______ early impact events.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"When the Moon was still forming, its surface was softer, and asteroid or meteoroid impacts would have left less of an impression; thus, evidence","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of early impacts may no longer be present.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["reflect","receive","evaluate","mimic"]},{"id":"a2dd51c1","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In most building demolitions, the building materials are destroyed and sent to landfills. City officials in Portland, Oregon, wanted to reduce this waste. The officials passed a law requiring demolition companies to deconstruct some buildings instead. Deconstruction involves carefully taking buildings apart piece by piece. Damage to the materials is avoided so that they can be reused in new constructions. A 2019 study found that 27 percent of materials from deconstructions in Portland were able to be reused. The remaining materials were processed for recycling instead of going to a landfill.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In most building demolitions, the building materials are destroyed and sent to landfills. City officials in Portland, Oregon, wanted to reduce this","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"waste. The officials passed a law requiring demolition companies to deconstruct some buildings instead. Deconstruction involves carefully","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"taking buildings apart piece by piece. Damage to the materials is avoided so that they can be reused in new constructions. A 2019 study found","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that 27 percent of materials from deconstructions in Portland were able to be reused. The remaining materials were processed for recycling","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"instead of going to a landfill.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To explain an effort made by the city of Portland to reduce demolition waste and some results of that effort","To show that popular support for measures that reduce demolition waste has increased since 2019","To argue that building deconstruction is not as effective as other measures at reducing demolition waste","To discuss laws aimed to reduce demolition waste in Portland and compare them to similar laws in other cities"]},{"id":"995358b4","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"In a 2022 study, Nicol ás M. Morato and colleagues attempted to resolve a long-standing paradox: although water is critical to most reactions that enable life, during the earliest stages of Earth’s history — when most of the planet’s surface was covered by oceans — the presence of water likely ______ the formation of proteins and other biomolecules that are found in all living organisms.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In a 2022 study, Nicolás M. Morato and colleagues attempted to resolve a long-standing paradox: although water is critical to most reactions","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that enable life, during the earliest stages of Earth’s history—when most of the planet’s surface was covered by oceans—the presence of water","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"likely ______ the formation of proteins and other biomolecules that are found in all living organisms.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["reflected","hampered","imitated","exploited"]},{"id":"ca47273b","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Biologist Jane Edgeloe and colleagues have located what is believed to be the largest individual plant in the world in the Shark Bay area of Australia. The plant is a type of seagrass called Posidonia australis, and it ______ approximately 200 square kilometers.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Biologist Jane Edgeloe and colleagues have located what is believed to be the largest individual plant in the world in the Shark Bay area of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Australia. The plant is a type of seagrass called Posidonia australis, and it ______ approximately 200 square kilometers.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["acknowledges","produces","spans","advances"]},{"id":"29741ebc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In the past, historians who wanted to examine Frederick Douglass’s diary and other personal papers had to visit the Library of Congress in Washington, DC, to view them on microfilm (film containing scaled-down reproductions of documents). But traveling to the library often added time and costs to research projects. Now, by going to the library’s website, researchers can access digitized versions of Douglass’s papers without physically going anywhere.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It gives information about a famous person.","It explains the meaning of a word.","It describes a debate among historians.","It summarizes an unexpected finding."],"underline":"(film containing scaled-down reproductions of documents).","underline_segments":["(film containing scaled-down reproductions of documents)."]},{"id":"82c05b34","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 The live music festival business is growing in event size and genre variety. With so many consumer options, organizers are finding ways to cement festival attendance as a special experience worth sharing. This phenomenon is linked to the growing “experiential economy,” where many find it gratifying to purchase lived experiences. To ensure a profitable event, venues need to consider the overall consumer experience, not just the band lineup. Text 2 Music festival appearances are becoming a more important part of musicians’ careers. One factor in this shift is the rising use of streaming services that allow access to huge numbers of songs for a monthly fee, subsequently reducing sales of full-length albums. With this shift in consumer behavior, musicians are increasingly dependent on revenue from live performances.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"The live music festival business is growing in event size and genre variety. With so many consumer options, organizers are finding ways to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"cement festival attendance as a special experience worth sharing. This phenomenon is linked to the growing “experiential economy,” where many","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"find it gratifying to purchase lived experiences. To ensure a profitable event, venues need to consider the overall consumer experience, not just","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the band lineup.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Music festival appearances are becoming a more important part of musicians’ careers. One factor in this shift is the rising use of streaming","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"services that allow access to huge numbers of songs for a monthly fee, subsequently reducing sales of full-length albums. With this shift in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"consumer behavior, musicians are increasingly dependent on revenue from live performances.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, both authors would most likely agree with which statement?","choices":["Consumers are more interested in paying subscription fees to stream music than in attending music festivals in person.","Consumers’ growing interest in purchasing experiences is mostly confined to the music industry.","Changing consumer behaviors are leading to changes in music-related businesses.","The rising consumer demand for live music festivals also generates higher demand for music streaming platforms."]},{"id":"2e744883","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Historians have argued that a crucial component of the Civil Rights Movement’s success in the 1960s was the Southern Christian Leadership Conference’s Citizen Education Program (CEP), which invited promising activists from across the South to its one-week training sessions in Dorchester, Georgia. Led by experienced organizers such as Dorothy Cotton and Septima Clark, CEP attendees — — more than 7,000 in all participated in workshops on topics ranging from public speaking to legal doctrine before returning home and using their newly acquired knowledge to spearhead local civil rights initiatives.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Historians have argued that a crucial component of the Civil Rights Movement’s success in the 1960s was the Southern Christian Leadership","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Conference’s Citizen Education Program (CEP), which invited promising activists from across the South to its one-week training sessions in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Dorchester, Georgia. Led by experienced organizers such as Dorothy Cotton and Septima Clark, CEP attendees—more than 7,000 in all—","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"participated in workshops on topics ranging from public speaking to legal doctrine before returning home and using their newly acquired","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"knowledge to spearhead local civil rights initiatives.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It underscores the extent of the CEP’s impact on the Civil Rights Movement of the 1960s.","It illustrates the CEP organizers efforts to educate participants on a wide variety of topics.","It suggests that CEP attendees held a diverse array of opinions about the Southern Christian Leadership Conference’s political philosophy.","It establishes that criticism of the CEP was limited to a few individuals in the Southern Christian Leadership Conference."],"underline":"— more than 7,000 in all —","underline_segments":["—more than 7,000 in all—"]},{"id":"271a5017","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Akwaeke Emezi’s 2019 novel Pet. Jam is a teenager who lives with her father, Aloe, and her mother, Bitter, who is a painter. Bitter finished the painting in the dark morning of a day — it was well past midnight when Jam heard the studio door creak open. She stared into the velvet black of her room and listened to her mother’s footsteps walking in her [mother] and Aloe’s bedroom. There was a weight thrumming through the floorboards in a low song, and that was how Jam knew the painting was done. Bitter’s feet were singing the news. ©2019 by Akwaeke Emezi","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Akwaeke Emezi’s 2019 novel Pet. Jam is a teenager who lives with her father, Aloe, and her mother, Bitter, who","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"is a painter.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Bitter finished the painting in the dark morning of a day—it was well past midnight when Jam heard the studio door creak open.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She stared into the velvet black of her room and listened to her mother’s footsteps walking in her [mother] and Aloe’s bedroom.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"There was a weight thrumming through the floorboards in a low song, and that was how Jam knew the painting was done. Bitter’s","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"feet were singing the news.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©2019 by Akwaeke Emezi","indent":4}],"question":"Which choice best states the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It indicates that Jam is more interested in music than in art.","It adds to the idea that Bitter’s footsteps reveal something to Jam.","It indicates that Bitter always sings when working on a painting.","It describes Aloe’s reaction upon seeing the painting for the first time."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Bitter’s","feet were singing the news."]},{"id":"db2da2bf","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"In 2019, 20 previously unknown moons were confirmed to be orbiting Saturn. Three of the moons have prograde orbits (orbiting in the direction the planet spins), and the other 17 have retrograde orbits (orbiting in the opposite direction of the planet’s spin). All but one of the 20 moons are thought to be remnants of bodies that orbited Saturn until they broke apart in collisions. Although the one exceptional moon orbits in the same direction as the planet’s spin, its orbit is highly eccentric compared to the rest, which may suggest that it has a different origin than the other 19 moons. Based on the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2019, 20 previously unknown moons were confirmed to be orbiting Saturn. Three of the moons have prograde orbits (orbiting in the direction","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the planet spins), and the other 17 have retrograde orbits (orbiting in the opposite direction of the planet’s spin). All but one of the 20 moons are","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"thought to be remnants of bodies that orbited Saturn until they broke apart in collisions. Although the one exceptional moon orbits in the same","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"direction as the planet’s spin, its orbit is highly eccentric compared to the rest, which may suggest that it has a different origin than the other 19","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"moons.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the text, which choice best describes the moon with the eccentric orbit?","choices":["It doesn’t have a retrograde orbit, but it likely has the same origin as the moons with retrograde orbits.","Its orbit is so tilted with respect to the other moons’ orbits that it’s neither prograde nor retrograde.","It has a prograde orbit that is likely the result of having collided with another body orbiting Saturn.","It has a prograde orbit and may not be a remnant of an earlier body that orbited Saturn."]},{"id":"a9390104","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"East Australian humpback whales migrate up to 10,000 kilometers each year to reach their breeding grounds. Researchers long believed that migrating whales live only on the extra energy they stored up during the feeding season. But marine biologist Vanessa Pirotta and her team aren’t so sure. They analyzed 20 years of observations of the migrating whales made by citizen scientists (members of the public who help collect data for scientific research). The team claims that the whales may not live only on their stored energy during migration.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"East Australian humpback whales migrate up to 10,000 kilometers each year to reach their breeding grounds. Researchers long believed that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"migrating whales live only on the extra energy they stored up during the feeding season. But marine biologist Vanessa Pirotta and her team aren’t","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"so sure. They analyzed 20 years of observations of the migrating whales made by citizen scientists (members of the public who help collect data","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"for scientific research). The team claims that the whales may not live only on their stored energy during migration.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the team’s claim?","choices":["Citizen scientists have observed many different types of marine animals feeding alongside the whales.","Citizen scientists have made many observations of the whales feeding as they migrate to their breeding grounds.","Citizen scientists have made more observations of the whales migrating to their breeding grounds than of the whales returning to their feeding grounds.","Citizen scientists have recently begun to observe the whales migrating to their breeding grounds earlier in the year."]},{"id":"98fd50f2","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Among the most visited art museums in the world, the Galleria dell’Accademia in Florence had approximately 1.7 million visitors in 2019. The Galleria dell’Accademia also offers virtual tours that art lovers can view online for free. Although there were initial concerns that people who viewed the virtual tours would then consider an in-person visit unnecessary, museum administrators claim that their surveys of in-person visitors show that those concerns were unjustified.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Among the most visited art museums in the world, the Galleria dell’Accademia in Florence had approximately 1.7 million visitors in 2019. The","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Galleria dell’Accademia also offers virtual tours that art lovers can view online for free. Although there were initial concerns that people who","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"viewed the virtual tours would then consider an in-person visit unnecessary, museum administrators claim that their surveys of in-person visitors","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"show that those concerns were unjustified.","indent":0}],"question":"Which statement, if true, would most directly support the administrators’ claim?","choices":["Many surveyed visitors to the Galleria dell’Accademia indicated that the virtual tours convinced them to plan an in-person visit.","Most surveyed visitors to the Galleria dell’Accademia indicated that they were unaware of the virtual tours before their first in-person visit.","Most surveyed visitors to the Galleria dell’Accademia indicated that they lived somewhere other than Florence.","Many surveyed visitors to the Galleria dell’Accademia indicated that they would likely view the virtual tours in order to reminisce about their in- person visit."]},{"id":"3cc2eacc","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"In a study of the mechanisms underlying associative memory —or the ability to learn and remember connections between inherently unrelated things — neuroscientists Kei Igarashi, Jasmine Chavez, and others presented mice with memory tests. The team discovered that fan cells, a type of cell found in the medial temporal lobe of the brain, are necessary for the acquisition of new associative memories. They also found that fan cell activity requires dopamine, a chemical the brain produces in response to pleasure and rewards. Consequently, receiving a reward should likely help to ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In a study of the mechanisms underlying associative memory—or the ability to learn and remember connections between inherently unrelated","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"things—neuroscientists Kei Igarashi, Jasmine Chavez, and others presented mice with memory tests. The team discovered that fan cells, a type","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of cell found in the medial temporal lobe of the brain, are necessary for the acquisition of new associative memories. They also found that fan","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"cell activity requires dopamine, a chemical the brain produces in response to pleasure and rewards. Consequently, receiving a reward should","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"likely help to ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["decrease an individual’s capacity to utilize dopamine.","increase an individual’s capacity to recognize differences between unrelated things.","increase an individual’s capacity to form associative memories.","decrease an individual’s capacity to create fan cells."]},{"id":"8a3ecac6","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"North American gray wolves usually have mixed gray and white fur, but some members of the species have a version of a gene, or gene variant, that gives them a mostly black coat instead. Sarah Cubaynes and her team studied twelve populations of North American gray wolves. They found that the black-furred wolves are more common in areas where outbreaks of distemper virus happen regularly. The team also discovered that the black-furred wolves are more likely to be immune to distemper than the gray-furred wolves are. Taken together, these findings suggest that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"North American gray wolves usually have mixed gray and white fur, but some members of the species have a version of a gene, or gene variant,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that gives them a mostly black coat instead. Sarah Cubaynes and her team studied twelve populations of North American gray wolves. They","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"found that the black-furred wolves are more common in areas where outbreaks of distemper virus happen regularly. The team also discovered","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that the black-furred wolves are more likely to be immune to distemper than the gray-furred wolves are. Taken together, these findings suggest","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["North American gray wolves experience more outbreaks of distemper virus than other wolf species do.","the gene variant that results in black fur may be linked to immunity to the distemper virus.","the average life span of gray wolves is likely to increase over time because of a particular gene variant.","gray-furred wolves will soon replace black-furred wolves across North America."]},{"id":"626a1308","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Data Sources for Neptune Temperature Analysis Instrument Observatory Data type Observation years TEXES (Texas Echelon Cross Echelle Spectrograph) Gemini Observatory spectroscopy 2007, 2019 T-ReCS (Thermal-Region Camera Spectrograph) Gemini Observatory infrared imaging 2007, 2010 LWS (Long Wavelength Spectrometer) Keck Observatory infrared imaging 2003 VISIR (VLT Imager and Spectrometer for mid-InfraRed) European Southern Observatory spectroscopy 2006 Julianne I. Moses and colleagues have reported that Neptune may have cooled significantly between 2003 and 2020. The team reached this conclusion by analyzing existing infrared imaging and spectroscopy data about the planet obtained from various instruments in different years. Of the team’s sources listed in the table, the earliest example of spectroscopy data included in the analysis was obtained in ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"table","title":"Data Sources for Neptune Temperature Analysis","headers":["Instrument","Observatory","Data type","Observation years"],"rows":[["TEXES (Texas Echelon Cross Echelle Spectrograph)","Gemini Observatory","spectroscopy","2007, 2019"],["T-ReCS (Thermal-Region Camera Spectrograph)","Gemini Observatory","infrared imaging","2007, 2010"],["LWS (Long Wavelength Spectrometer)","Keck Observatory","infrared imaging","2003"],["VISIR (VLT Imager and Spectrometer for mid-InfraRed)","European Southern Observatory","spectroscopy","2006"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Julianne I. Moses and colleagues have reported that Neptune may have cooled significantly between 2003 and 2020. The team reached this conclusion by analyzing existing infrared imaging and spectroscopy data about the planet obtained from various instruments in different years. Of the team’s sources listed in the table, the earliest example of spectroscopy data included in the analysis was obtained in ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the text?","choices":["2007 using TEXES at the Gemini Observatory.","2007 using T-ReCS at the Gemini Observatory.","2006 using VISIR at the European Southern Observatory.","2003 using LWS at the W.M. Keck Observatory."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Data Sources for","Neptune Temperature Analysis"]},{"id":"7254379e","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Some residents in a neighborhood in Atlanta recently founded a community garden inside a local park. The residents agreed to volunteer to take care of the garden together. Students at a local high school surveyed some of the volunteers as part of a project to understand the impact of the new garden.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Some residents in a neighborhood in Atlanta recently founded a community garden inside a local park. The residents agreed to volunteer to take","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"care of the garden together. Students at a local high school surveyed some of the volunteers as part of a project to understand the impact of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"new garden. The students concluded that the new garden benefited the community overall by fostering connections and relationships between","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the volunteers and other residents of the neighborhood who weren’t volunteering at the garden.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from a survey respondent would best illustrate the students’ conclusion?","choices":["“Our first challenge was deciding what plants would be most suitable to the climate and soil here in Atlanta. We needed plants that could survive the hot and humid summers.”","“We’re lucky to have a few expert gardeners living in the neighborhood. Some volunteers and I have gone to them a few times with questions, and they’ve been eager to help us and to learn more about the project.”","“I love getting the opportunity to be outside and around nature, especially on days when the weather is nice.”","“My favorite thing about the garden is the feeling of pride I get when I walk by each day. As I see the plants growing, I feel good knowing I had a small part in creating this beautiful space in the neighborhood.”"]},{"id":"3595a991","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In 1930, Japanese American artist Chiura Obata depicted the natural beauty of Yosemite National Park in two memorable woodcuts: Evening at Carl Inn and Lake Basin in the High Sierra. In 2019, ______ exhibited alongside 150 of Obata’s other works in a single-artist show at the Smithsonian American Art Museum.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 1930, Japanese American artist Chiura Obata depicted the natural beauty of Yosemite National Park in two memorable woodcuts: Evening at","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Carl Inn and Lake Basin in the High Sierra. In 2019, ______ exhibited alongside 150 of Obata’s other works in a single-artist show at the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Smithsonian American Art Museum.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["it was","they were","this was","some were"]},{"id":"1f39ab8b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In the novel Things Fall Apart by Chinua Achebe, Okonkwo is a leader of Umuofia (a fictional Nigerian clan) and takes pride in his culture’s traditions. However, when the arrival of European missionaries brings changes to Umuofia, the novel asks a central question: How ______","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Umuofia’s traditions will be affected.","will Umuofia’s traditions be affected.","Umuofia’s traditions will be affected?","will Umuofia’s traditions be affected?"]},{"id":"940ff6f7","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Jamaican British artist Willard Wigan is known for his remarkable ______ so small that they are best viewed through a microscope, Wigan’s sculptures are made from tiny natural materials, such as spiderweb strands.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Jamaican British artist Willard Wigan is known for his remarkable ______ so small that they are best viewed through a microscope, Wigan’s","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sculptures are made from tiny natural materials, such as spiderweb strands.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["microsculptures creations","microsculptures, creations","microsculptures. Creations","microsculptures and creations"]},{"id":"37e5c794","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Despite being cheap, versatile, and easy to produce, ______ they are made from nonrenewable petroleum, and most do not biodegrade in landfills.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Despite being cheap, versatile, and easy to produce, ______ they are made from nonrenewable petroleum, and most do not biodegrade in landfills.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["there are two problems associated with commercial plastics:","two problems are associated with commercial plastics:","commercial plastics two associated problems are that","commercial plastics have two associated problems:"]},{"id":"89fbc3eb","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"The Mission 66 initiative, which was approved by Congress in 1956, represented a major investment in the infrastructure of overburdened national ______ it prioritized physical improvements to the parks’ roads, utilities, employee housing, and visitor facilities while also establishing educational programming for the public.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The Mission 66 initiative, which was approved by Congress in 1956, represented a major investment in the infrastructure of overburdened","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"national ______ it prioritized physical improvements to the parks’ roads, utilities, employee housing, and visitor facilities while also establishing","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"educational programming for the public.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["parks and","parks","parks;","parks,"]},{"id":"5670a657","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"During the decades-long movement to codify the rights of Latinos in the US, certain events were pivotal: the founding of social justice group the League of United Latin American Citizens in ______ Katzenbach v. Morgan court decision in 1966, which affirmed the rights of Latino voters, is another such event.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"During the decades-long movement to codify the rights of Latinos in the US, certain events were pivotal: the founding of social justice group the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"League of United Latin American Citizens in ______Katzenbach v. Morgan court decision in 1966, which affirmed the rights of Latino voters, is","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"another such event.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["1929. For one, the","1929, for one, the","1929 for one, the","1929, for one. The"]},{"id":"db8fe023","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"A potter choosing which type of clay to use for a piece considers two key factors: the desired look of the piece and its intended use. ______ earthenware clay is often used for decorative pieces because of its rustic look. This type of clay is not often used in industrial settings, though, because it is less durable than other clays.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"A potter choosing which type of clay to use for a piece considers two key factors: the desired look of the piece and its intended use. ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"earthenware clay is often used for decorative pieces because of its rustic look. This type of clay is not often used in industrial settings, though,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"because it is less durable than other clays.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In other words,","Regardless,","In conclusion,","For example,"]},{"id":"47547d07","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In June, female loggerhead sea turtles will swim back to the sandy beaches where they were born to lay eggs of their own. First, the turtle will dig her nest in the sand. ______ she will lay up to 100 eggs in the nest. Finally, she will cover it all with sand, before returning to the ocean.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In June, female loggerhead sea turtles will swim back to the sandy beaches where they were born to lay eggs of their own. First, the turtle will dig","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"her nest in the sand. ______ she will lay up to 100 eggs in the nest. Finally, she will cover it all with sand, before returning to the ocean.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["By contrast,","Similarly,","Next,","For example,"]},{"id":"63a4fa29","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: In 2013, archaeologists studied cat bone fragments they had found in the ruins of Quanhucun, a Chinese farming village. The fragments were estimated to be 5,300 years old. A chemical analysis of the fragments revealed that the cats had consumed large amounts of grain. The grain consumption is evidence that the Quanhucun cats may have been domesticated. The student wants to present the Quanhucun study and its conclusions.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"In 2013, archaeologists studied cat bone fragments they had found in the ruins of Quanhucun, a Chinese farming village.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The fragments were estimated to be 5,300 years old.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"A chemical analysis of the fragments revealed that the cats had consumed large amounts of grain.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The grain consumption is evidence that the Quanhucun cats may have been domesticated.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["As part of a 2013 study of cat domestication, a chemical analysis was conducted on cat bone fragments found in Quanhucun, China.","A 2013 analysis of cat bone fragments found in Quanhucun, China, suggests that cats there may have been domesticated 5,300 years ago.","In 2013, archaeologists studied what cats in Quanhucun, China, had eaten more than 5,000 years ago.","Cat bone fragments estimated to be 5,300 years old were found in Quanhucun, China, in 2013."]},{"id":"bb275f0d","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Cities tend to have a wide range of flowering vegetation in parks, yards, and gardens. This vegetation provides a varied diet for honeybees, strengthening bees’ immune systems. On average, 62.5 percent of bees in an urban area will survive a harsh winter. Rural areas are often dominated by monoculture crops such as corn or wheat. On average, only 40 percent of honeybees in a rural area will survive a harsh winter. The student wants to make and support a generalization about honeybees.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Cities tend to have a wide range of flowering vegetation in parks, yards, and gardens.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"This vegetation provides a varied diet for honeybees, strengthening bees’ immune systems.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"On average, 62.5 percent of bees in an urban area will survive a harsh winter.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Rural areas are often dominated by monoculture crops such as corn or wheat.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"On average, only 40 percent of honeybees in a rural area will survive a harsh winter.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Cities tend to have a wider range of flowering vegetation than do rural areas, which are often dominated by monoculture crops.","In urban areas, over 60 percent of honeybees, on average, will survive a harsh winter, whereas in rural areas, only 40 percent will.","The strength of honeybees’ immune systems depends on what the bees eat, and a varied diet is more available to bees in an urban area than to those in a rural area.","Honeybees are more likely to thrive in cities than in rural areas because the varied diet available in urban areas strengthens the bees’ immune systems."]},{"id":"39ccb463","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: The Atlantic Monthly magazine was first published in 1857. The magazine focused on politics, art, and literature. In 2019, historian Cathryn Halverson published the book Faraway Women and the “Atlantic Monthly.” Its subject is female authors whose autobiographies appeared in the magazine in the early 1900s. One of the authors discussed is Juanita Harrison. The student wants to introduce Cathryn Halverson’s book to an audience already familiar with the Atlantic Monthly.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The Atlantic Monthly magazine was first published in 1857.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The magazine focused on politics, art, and literature.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"In 2019, historian Cathryn Halverson published the book Faraway Women and the “Atlantic Monthly.”","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Its subject is female authors whose autobiographies appeared in the magazine in the early 1900s.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"One of the authors discussed is Juanita Harrison.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Cathryn Halverson’s Faraway Women and the “Atlantic Monthly” discusses female authors whose autobiographies appeared in the magazine in the early 1900s.","A magazine called the Atlantic Monthly, referred to in Cathryn Halverson’s book title, was first published in 1857.","Faraway Women and the “Atlantic Monthly” features contributors to the Atlantic Monthly, first published in 1857 as a magazine focusing on politics, art, and literature.","An author discussed by Cathryn Halverson is Juanita Harrison, whose autobiography appeared in the Atlantic Monthly in the early 1900s."]},{"id":"e2693197","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Oracles of the Pink Universe was a 2021 exhibition at the Denver Museum of Art in Colorado. It featured eight artworks by South African artist Simphiwe Ndzube. One of these works is a painting titled Assertion of Will. Assertion of Will depicts three standing figures. The figures wear clothing made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting’s canvas. The student wants to describe how fabric is used in Assertion of Will.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Oracles of the Pink Universe was a 2021 exhibition at the Denver Museum of Art in Colorado.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"It featured eight artworks by South African artist Simphiwe Ndzube.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"One of these works is a painting titled Assertion of Will.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Assertion of Will depicts three standing figures.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The figures wear clothing made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting’s canvas.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["In Assertion of Will, the figures’ clothing is made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting’s canvas.","The exhibition Oracles of the Pink Universe featured artworks by artist Simphiwe Ndzube.","Depicting three standing, clothed figures, Assertion of Will is a painting by Simphiwe Ndzube.","Simphiwe Ndzube’s Assertion of Will was one of eight artworks exhibited in Oracles of the Pink Universe at the Denver Museum of Art."]}];
